UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Seven of Cups is the absolute archetype of the "Infinite Input Field"—a state of total, unconstrained imaginative expansion where the consciousness is presented with an overwhelming array of potential realities, desires, and paths. Moving beyond the reclaimed history of the Six, the Seven of Cups marks the point where the soul, now reconnected to its internal source, faces the daunting task of choice within an environment of limitless options. Visually depicted as a figure standing before seven mysterious cups floating in a cloud, each containing a different image or possibility, this archetype signifies a phase where your psychic field is saturated with potential. Within the complex architecture of your manifestation process, this is the stage of "radical brainstorming" or "probabilistic exploration." It is the moment when you recognize that every choice you make collapses the wave function of your life, but before that collapse occurs, you are free to explore every conceivable iteration of your desire. When the Seven of Cups appears, your system is being subjected to a high-volume data-stream of "what-ifs," and your primary challenge is to maintain your sovereign center amidst the chaotic magnetism of these competing visions. It serves as a diagnostic tool for your desires: are you pursuing these paths because they are authentic expressions of your soul-alignment, or are they mere illusions crafted by the ego to distract you from the discipline of actualized creation? You are invited to survey this vast internal landscape with the discernment of an architect, acknowledging that while you have the energy to pursue many avenues, true power lies in the strategic selection and sustained commitment to a singular, high-utility trajectory. To inhabit the Seven of Cups is to master the art of discerning "vision" from "fantasy"—the former being a coherent, grounded blueprint for your future, and the latter being a low-vibration, ephemeral distraction that consumes your precious processing bandwidth without ever producing a stable, real-world result. It is the cosmic test of your focus; you are asked to sort through the noise, recognize the common thread of truth running through your varied interests, and begin the necessary, ego-stripping work of pruning the excess so that your deepest intent may finally have the room to take root in the soil of reality.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Seven of Cups appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "manifestation paralysis" or "probabilistic exhaustion"—a state where the infinite input field has curdled into a suffocating, low-vibration fog of indecision, fragmented focus, and compulsive escapism. The reversal suggests that you have been so thoroughly seduced by the siren call of your own multifaceted fantasies that you have completely lost touch with the structural requirements of your present-day existence. You are essentially "drunk on the idea of yourself," running thousands of competing, high-latency simulations of success, glory, and transformation, but failing to execute on even the most basic, foundational steps required to bring those visions into the material realm. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: your aspirations are operating in a high-frequency, non-local imaginative space, while your physical life is stagnating in a state of high-entropy chaos. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "multiverse of mediocrity," where you dabble in everything and master nothing, leaving you with a profound, chronic sense of fragmentation, restlessness, and intellectual burnout. The reversed Seven of Cups exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the terror of making a "wrong" choice, or worse, the fear that even if you committed to one path, your reality wouldn’t measure up to the idealized fantasies you have constructed in your head. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these high-volume, low-utility scripts, purge the distractions that have cluttered your psychic field, and initiate a "forced closure" of all non-essential imaginative loops. It is a demand to stop the performative act of "dreaming" and start the disciplined, often unglamorous work of choosing. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical prioritization—clearing the board of every option that does not directly serve your core soul-intent. It is a call to reclaim your agency, to accept the finality of choice, and to understand that by choosing one path, you are not losing the others; you are finally beginning the process of actually inhabiting your life, rather than merely spectating the thousands of ways your life could have been lived.'
WHERE id = 7;
